{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Young II (Thomas Young, 1800)."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"youngII"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV","text":"WellTemperament","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament"},{"kind":"text","text":" { "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"get"},{"kind":"text","text":" }"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Six consecutive fifths from C to F♯ — C→G, G→D, D→A, A→E, E→B, B→F♯ — are each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"narrowed by ⅙ of the Pythagorean comma, equal to 2^(13\/6)\/3 ≈ 698.045 cents."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The remaining six fifths are pure (3:2). The circle closes exactly.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The tempered fifth size is identical to Vallotti, but the tempered segment runs","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from C through F♯ (six sharps) rather than from F through B (six naturals\/flats).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Published in ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Philosophical Transactions of the Royal Society"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" 90 (1800).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/TuningSystem"]]},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"property","roleHeading":"Type Property","extendedModule":"IvorTuning","modules":[{"name":"IvorTuning"}],"title":"youngII","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind"